A||||5||Klown||Clutch chatter?||||5||
Z||000000||Klown||10-30-2001||02:56 AM||||Hey guys, my mechanic just finished installing my new clutch on Friday.  Whenever I engage the clutch on start ups (low speed in first gear) I seem to get a little bit of chatter.  Is this because the clutch isn't broken in yet or is it because this clutch is a six spring design instead of four?||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||10-30-2001||08:52 AM||||my 4 puck chattered.. what friction material is on the dics? if it's a 6 spring it'll chatter less.. how was the flywheel surfaced? what pressure plate are you using?<P>this chatterd like hell but would hold well over 300lbft of torque...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fst4puck.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>0-60 in 4.91<P> <A HREF="http://www.1fst2m6.com" TARGET=_blank>www.1fst2m6.com</A>  - underconstruction - but check it out anywho...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Klown||10-30-2001||09:29 PM||||Well I'm pretty sure that the surface material was organic and that the pressure plate was close to stock.  As far as how the flywheel was resurfaced, I don't know.  I didn't even realize there was more than one way to resurface it.  I wish I could remember the brand name.  I only remember that it seemed to be a "heavy duty" organic clutch with six springs instead of four.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DR650SE||10-30-2001||11:46 PM||||One one of my cars I installed the Kevlar high power racing clutch.  It is a six spring design.  How bad will this chatter.  I know that it will just how bad.  I got a Z racing clutch (zoom? not sure its purple and was on the car when i got it) on my other car and it chatters.  Thanks all!<BR>                     Kindest Regards,<BR>                        Dan Tillman<P>------------------<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||11
Z||000004||1FST2M6||11-01-2001||09:15 AM||||organincs should'nt chatter unless it's a solid hub...  if the flywheel was turned on a dedecated machine it should be fine.. there were a couple times i didnt care about mine and was changing just the disc pads and just hit the flywheel with an abrasive disc on a die grinder.. that gave me an uneven surface which lead to even more chatter and less disc pad life but at $60 for new ones and to be able to launch insanly i really didn't care... since a resurface would run $50 and the ceramics just destroyed the flywheel --anyway. sorry off the subject..  does your dash shake or does your pedal seem notchy? ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Klown||11-03-2001||05:24 AM||||Actually the pedal feels fine.  I do seem to feel a little more vibration through it in first gear though.  I'm not sure if it's new or if it was alway there but I just never felt it before.  <BR>The car does seem to rattle a little and I'm sure that wasn't the case before.  It only happens when starting from a complete stop and in the lower rpm's.  It's tricky to get it to slip smoothly whereas before I had no problem.  I'll have to make sure with my mechanic as to whether or not the disk was organic.||||reg||1
